# OAuth client ID from Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials
# -> Create credentials -> OAuth client ID -> Web application.
# Add your origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173) to "Authorised JavaScript origins".
#
# You can also paste the client ID into Settings inside the app at runtime,
# which is stored in localStorage and does not need a rebuild.
#
# This file is for a local .env, which is gitignored. The client ID the
# deployed site is built with lives in .env.production, which is committed —
# a client ID is not a secret. The client *secret* is not used by this app at
# all and should not be put in either file.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
